  "worked_solution": "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)\u21d4Q(x)\u2261(P(x)\u2227Q(x))\u2228(\u00acP(x)\u2227\u00acQ(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d4Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/5dfcb1cff13cc5f5b6dcfa42a7e1d08184e54a7edd91717b795692068db37121.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/3c4b6cd6b5649a18bd768b3086ccef5a995f9745a9ce90160507c9d92f46f8dc.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/62373d6926552c34849e91115163dba42483c6259482bc4893704af570749c89.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)\u21d4Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099768/assets/252c206ca03b339c4bb186c95d21cd26110fc902f0ab9bca6df2d8d594aacba5.png)",
